# SQL Migration Rules

## Naming

```
backend/src/migrations/NNN_description.sql
```

- `NNN` = next sequential number after the highest existing file (currently up to `020`)
- `description` = lowercase, underscores, brief (e.g. `021_habit_streaks`)
- **Never edit existing migration files** — they are append-only

Check the next number:
```bash
ls backend/src/migrations/ | sort | tail -3
```

## Template

```sql
-- Migration: NNN_description
-- Purpose: [one-line reason]
-- Created: YYYY-MM-DD

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS my_table (
  id          BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  user_id     TEXT NOT NULL,           -- Firebase UID or DV guest ID (always TEXT)
  data        JSONB,
  created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_my_table_user_id ON my_table(user_id);
```

## Rules

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Idempotent** | `IF NOT EXISTS` / `IF EXISTS` everywhere |
| **user_id is TEXT** | Firebase UIDs and DV guest IDs are strings — never integer FK |
| **JSONB for flexible data** | Prefer `JSONB` over many individual columns for user content |
| **Index user_id** | Always add an index on `user_id` for any new table |
| **Timestamps** | `created_at` + `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()` on every new table |
| **No passwords** | Auth is Firebase / DV token — never store passwords |
| **No drops without comment** | `DROP`/`TRUNCATE` needs a clear reason comment |

## Running

```bash
cd backend
node src/migrate.js
```

## After the Migration

Update storage modules to use the new schema:

1. **`backend/src/storage_pg.js`** — add the PostgreSQL implementation
2. **`backend/src/storage.js`** — add the equivalent JSON-file fallback (same function signature)
3. Register the new functions on the `db` export in **`backend/src/db.js`** if needed

Both implementations must have identical function signatures so the abstraction layer in `db.js` works without modification.
